<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108722" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόλογ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>held accountable</i> or
				<i>liable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tab.Heracl.
				1.138
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				30.15
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γως</span>
			<i>responsibly, as a responsible person,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμνύω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					87.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>reckoned to one's account,</i> either to one's credit or
			against one, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέν σοι ὑ. τίθεμαι
			ἐάν</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				349c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				36.48
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ ἀδίκως τούτοις φημὶ ἂν εἶναι
					ὑ. τὴν ἐκείνων φυγήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					28.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲν τὴν ἡμετέραν ἡλικίαν ὑ.
					ποιούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>La.</u>
					189b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
